## Ownership Principles

### Company Ownership

MedSync owns all IP created by employees:
- During employment
- Within scope of employment
- Using company resources
- Related to company business

This includes:
- Inventions
- Discoveries
- Improvements
- Software
- Documentation
- Designs

### Prior Inventions

| Requirement | Process |
|-------------|---------|
| Disclosure | Prior to employment |
| Documentation | Exhibit to employment agreement |
| Exclusion | Listed items excluded |

### Personal Projects

| Allowed | Conditions |
|---------|------------|
| Outside Work | Not using company time |
| Own Resources | Not using company equipment |
| Unrelated | Not competing with company |
| Disclosed | Prior written approval |

---

## Employee Obligations

### Assignment

All employees must:
- Assign all work-related IP to MedSync
- Sign IP assignment agreement
- Cooperate with patent applications
- Execute necessary documents
- Not claim personal ownership

### Disclosure

Employees must promptly disclose:
- New inventions or discoveries
- Improvements to existing products
- Potential patentable innovations
- Trade secret developments

### Disclosure Process

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1 | Complete Invention Disclosure Form |
| 2 | Submit to Legal |
| 3 | Initial review (7 days) |
| 4 | IP Committee evaluation (30 days) |
| 5 | Decision and next steps |

### Confidentiality

Employees must:
- Protect company trade secrets
- Not disclose confidential information
- Follow security policies
- Return materials upon termination
- Maintain confidentiality post-employment

